issues.description:
**Goal:** Update the unit test suite to set `TenantContext` for tests that exercise tenant-scoped entities. After the Cosmos migration code landed (per work items #1333, #1334, #1335, #1336, #1339), 85 of 229 unit tests fail with `System.InvalidOperationException: No tenant in scope. Call TenantContext.Use(customerId) first.` This is not a bug in the migration — it is the tests not yet aware of the new tenant-routing model.

**Baseline (as of this issue):**
- Total: 229 tests
- Passing: 138 (all global-DB entities — `Lookup`, `Employee` identity tests, system telemetry)
- Failing: 85 (every test that touches a tenant-scoped entity)
- Skipped: 6

**Scope of this issue:**

*Test infrastructure:*
- Add a `TenantTestBase` class under `ORBIT.Test.Unit/` that sets up `TenantContext.Use(<seeded test customer id>)` in `[TestInitialize]` and disposes it in `[TestCleanup]`. Pick a customer id that is reliably seeded in the local Mongo container (the same one currently used for tenant-data tests).
- Have failing test classes inherit from `TenantTestBase`. The `using` block disappears from individual tests; the base class handles it once per test method automatically.

*Test class updates:*
- Sweep the failing test classes and either inherit from `TenantTestBase` (preferred) or add explicit `using ( TenantContext.Use( ... ) )` blocks per method. Test files affected (not exhaustive — confirm against full failure list):
  - `ORBIT.Test.Unit/Customer/Roles.cs`
  - `ORBIT.Test.Unit/Customer/Tasks.cs`
  - `ORBIT.Test.Unit/Customer/TaskAudits.cs`
  - `ORBIT.Test.Unit/Customer/Layers.cs`
  - `ORBIT.Test.Unit/Customer/CustomerReports.cs`
  - `ORBIT.Test.Unit/Customer/WorkSites.cs`
  - `ORBIT.Test.Unit/CheckIn/*.cs`
  - `ORBIT.Test.Unit/Notification/*.cs`
  - `ORBIT.Test.Unit/PositionAssignments.cs` (touches Tda)
  - Anything else surfaced when re-running the suite after the base class lands

*Slash-command update:*
- Update `.claude/commands/test.md` so the `/test` skill generates the `TenantTestBase` inheritance (or the explicit `using` block) by default for any new test against a tenant-scoped entity. Add a "Category E — Tenant-scoped CRUD" section to the entity-categories list with the pattern.

**Out of scope for this issue:**
- Playwright tests — those are blocked separately by a Redis configuration issue in the local `orbit-web` container (it tries to authenticate against the production Azure Redis for DataProtection key storage). That is unrelated to the migration and tracked separately.
- The 138 passing tests — leave them alone; they don't touch tenant entities.

**Verification:**
- Re-run `/runtests` after the changes.
- Target: zero "No tenant in scope" failures. The remaining failures (if any) should be unrelated to tenant routing.

**Pattern reference:**

```csharp
// ORBIT.Test.Unit/TenantTestBase.cs
public abstract class TenantTestBase
{
    private const string TestCustomerId = "<seeded test customer id>";
    private IDisposable _tenantScope;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void TenantSetup()
    {
        _tenantScope = TenantContext.Use( TestCustomerId );
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void TenantTeardown()
    {
        _tenantScope?.Dispose();
    }
}

// then on a failing test class:
[TestClass]
public class RoleTest : TenantTestBase
{
    [TestMethod]
    public void Role_Save_TogglesCanManageTask()
    {
        // Tenant is already set by TenantTestBase
        var role = CustomerRole.FetchBy( true ).FirstOrDefault();
        ...
    }
}
```

**Reference:** `CosmosDB-Migration-Design.md` — see the `orbit-tenant-{customerId}` section and the Code Changes Required #3 (Tenant resolver in the Web layer).
